Phoenix-RTOS: add a dedicated platform branch to SDL's CMake configuration.

Without this, a cross build (CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME=Generic) matches no platform
branch, so CheckPTHREAD is never called and the configure aborts at the
"Threads ... may not be disabled" gate. Making it *look* like Linux instead is
worse: the UNIX/Linux branch runs host-toolchain probes (X11/Wayland/KMSDRM/
udev/dbus/GL/ALSA) that leak host include paths such as -I/usr/include into
every subsequent try_compile and break the cross build.

This branch wires only the portable subsystems libphoenix already backs: the
unix (CLOCK_MONOTONIC) timer and pthread threads. Video, audio, joystick,
filesystem, loadso, etc. fall back to SDL's dummy drivers automatically. The
phoenix video/input/audio drivers get wired into this same branch by later
patches. Enabled by -DPHOENIX=ON (set by the port).

--- a/CMakeLists.txt	2025-02-02 00:56:51.000000000 +0100
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt	2026-08-04 22:48:09.144475192 +0200
@@ -1452,6 +1452,28 @@
   CheckPTHREAD()
   CheckLibUnwind()
 
+elseif(PHOENIX)
+  # Phoenix-RTOS is a POSIX-ish RTOS. libphoenix supplies the libc, libc-
+  # integrated pthreads and clock_gettime(). We deliberately do NOT run the
+  # generic UNIX/Linux host detection below (X11/Wayland/KMSDRM/udev/dbus/GL/
+  # ALSA/...): those probe the *host* toolchain and leak host include paths
+  # (e.g. -I/usr/include) into every subsequent try_compile, which breaks the
+  # cross build. Phase 1 wires only the portable subsystems that libphoenix
+  # already backs: pthread threads and the unix (CLOCK_MONOTONIC) timer. Every
+  # other subsystem (video, audio, joystick, filesystem, loadso, ...) falls
+  # back to SDL's dummy driver automatically further down. The phoenix video/
+  # input/audio drivers are wired in by later patches (phase 2+).
+  if(SDL_TIMERS)
+    set(SDL_TIMER_UNIX 1)
+    file(GLOB TIMER_SOURCES ${SDL2_SOURCE_DIR}/src/timer/unix/*.c)
+    list(APPEND SOURCE_FILES ${TIMER_SOURCES})
+    set(HAVE_SDL_TIMERS TRUE)
+    if(SDL_CLOCK_GETTIME)
+      set(HAVE_CLOCK_GETTIME 1)
+    endif()
+  endif()
+  CheckPTHREAD()
+
 elseif(UNIX AND NOT APPLE AND NOT RISCOS AND NOT HAIKU)
   if(SDL_AUDIO)
     if(SYSV5 OR SOLARIS OR HPUX)
